      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Opportunistic infection and neoplasia involving the gastrointestinal tract are common in AIDS patients. Life-threatening complications of this involvement may occur, requiring urgent diagnosis and therapy. We review the clinical presentation and approaches to management of AIDS-related gastrointestinal emergencies."},
